    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression and live character vitals, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.7 — Live character vitals[/h1]\n[b]Added[/b]\n[list]\n[*]A live character dashboard export: every online player gets a heartbeat roughly every ten real seconds, written to Lua/vitals/<username>.json.\n[*]Health overall and per body part, with the wounds on each, plus a flat wound list carrying part, type, severity and whether it has been treated.\n[*]Trained skills with progress towards the next level, and the full moodle stack — hunger, thirst, fatigue, endurance, stress, panic, boredom, unhappiness, pain, wetness, drunkenness, temperature, sickness and cold.\n[*]The equipped weapon (condition, sharpness, ammo, chamber, jam, attachments) and worn clothing per garment (condition, holes, bite and scratch defence).\n[*]Body temperature, bite and scratch protection per part, encumbrance, the quickload hotbar, and recently learned recipes.\n[/list]\n[b]Changed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]This shipped as the separate PZServerPulse mod before. It is part of Knox Relay now — if you run both, drop PZServerPulse from Mods=, or two mods will write the same data.\n[*]Skill levels are looked up once and shared between the heartbeat and player_stats.json, which is itself unchanged.\n[/list]\n[b]Notes[/b]\nOnly online players produce heartbeats, so a missing file means \"not logged in\" rather than a broken bridge. If your build does not expose the recipe-learned event the mod still loads and logs a warning; only the recent recipes panel stays empty. Where the vitals/ directory cannot be created the mod falls back to a flat Lua/vitals_<username>.json instead of dropping the heartbeat."
}
